.SH "NAME"
pcre2_maketables_free \- free character tables
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

void\fP \f(CBpcre2_maketables_free\fP\f(CR(pcre2_general_context *\fP\f(CIgcontext\fP\f(CR,
                           const uint8_t *\fP\f(CItables\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function discards a set of character tables that were created by a call
to \f(CBpcre2_maketables()\fP.
.sp
The \f(CIgcontext\fP parameter should match what was used in that call to
account for any custom allocators that might be in use; if it is \f(CBNULL\fP
the system \f(CBfree\fP\f(CR()\fP is used.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page.